{
  "id": "04-gifts-for-service",
  "title": "Gifts for the Common Good",
  "tenet": "Receive and serve",
  "durationMs": 41952,
  "audioAsset": "kingdom/04-gifts-for-service.mp3",
  "transcriptAsset": "assets/kingdom/04-gifts-for-service.json",
  "text": "A boy saw his father share a basket of fruit with the whole street. The gift was real because it reached someone hungry. In the Kingdom, the Spirit gives gifts for the good of others. We may pray for discernment, faith, healing, prophecy, and strength to serve. We receive every gift with humility, test what we believe we hear, and never use another person's need as a stage. The Spirit also grows joy, peace, patience, and love in ordinary life. These blessings are grace, not a prize we can demand. Ask God which person needs your attention. Ask for the gift that would help you serve faithfully. Then give what you have, even if it seems small.",
